session "DFS_Skeletons" in DFS = "Directed_Set_Graphs" +
  description \<open>Generic depth-first search skeletons.

    DFS_Skeleton is the bare skeleton: a stack-based search over a Pair_Graph_Specs adjacency map,
    parameterized by callbacks, with its termination argument and the invariants (seen/finished,
    the stack shape) proved once and for all. DFS_Skel_More duplicates it solely to add an on_push
    callback, applied to the freshly-pushed state in the descend step, and DFS_Skel_More_Refine
    moves the adjacency map into the state so a callback may prune it, proving the loop equivalent
    to the one that reads a fixed map.

    Kept as a light session of its own so that consumers needing only a DFS skeleton -- e.g. the
    directed-cycle detection in Directed_Cycle_DFS, or an external development such as a datalog
    foundedness check -- need not depend on Graph_Algorithms_Dev, which pulls in
    Verified_SAT_Based_AI_Planning, BFS and Bellman-Ford.\<close>
  theories
    DFS_Skeleton
    DFS_Skel_More
    DFS_Skel_More_Refine

session "Directed_Cycle_DFS" in Directed_Cycles = "DFS_Skeletons" +
  description \<open>Directed-cycle detection by depth-first search.

    DFS_DirCycle is the single-root directed-cycle detector on the DFS_Skeletons skeleton: a cycle
    exists below the root iff the search meets a back edge, i.e. an edge into a seen but unfinished
    vertex.\<close>
  theories
    DFS_DirCycle

